Supermarket Sales EDA 
Exploratory Data Analysis of supermarket sales data using Python, Pandas, NumPy, and Matplotlib.
📊 Project Overview 
This project explores supermarket sales data to understand sales performance, customer behavior, product lines, payment methods, and other business-related patterns.
The analysis includes data inspection, cleaning, feature creation, filtering, aggregation, and visualization.
🗂️ Dataset 
The dataset contains 1,000 sales transactions and 17 columns, including information such as:
Branch City Customer Type Gender Product Line Unit Price Quantity Tax Total Date Time Payment Rating Gross Income 
🔍 Analysis Performed Checked dataset shape and data types Inspected missing values and duplicates Generated descriptive statistics Created date-based features Analyzed sales by product line Compared sales across branches and cities Analyzed customer types and gender Explored payment methods Analyzed customer ratings Used filtering, value_counts(), groupby(), and aggregation Created visualizations to identify patterns and trends 🛠️ Tools & Libraries Python Pandas NumPy Matplotlib Google Colab Jupyter Notebook
📈 Key Insights 
The analysis provides insights into:
Product-line performance Branch and city-level sales patterns Customer demographics Payment method preferences Quantity and revenue patterns Customer ratings Gross income and overall sales performance 📁 Repository Contents Supermarket_sales_EDA.ipynb — Complete exploratory data analysis notebook README.md — Project documentation supermarket_sales.csv — Dataset used for the analysis 🎯 Purpose 
This project was created as part of my Data Science learning journey to practice practical Exploratory Data Analysis and build a portfolio using real-world sales data.
